  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Civil Society Regional Partnerships in favour of the ratification of the African Disability Protocol (ADP).</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;Objectives of the regional action:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;All persons with disabilities in Malawi, Zambia, and Zimbabwe enjoy human rights and other fundamental freedoms enshrined in CRPD and national constitutions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;Outcome objectives include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;&lt;strong&gt;Outcome 1 &lt;/strong&gt;- Expedition of the ratification, domestication and implementation of ADP and associated instruments in Malawi, Zambia, and Zimbabwe,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;&lt;strong&gt;Outcome 2 &lt;/strong&gt;- OPDs&#xbf; and CSOs&#xbf; internal governance, transparency and organisational support is improved,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#xb7;&lt;strong&gt;Outcome 3 &lt;/strong&gt;- Participation of OPDs and CBOs to elevate disability inclusion issues in the development processes and implementation of rights of all persons with disabilities in Malawi, Zambia and Zimbabwe is improved.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
